KelpServer (crates/server, crates/protocol) was extracted from Kelpmux
(https://github.com/joanfabregat/kelpmux) at commit eb31da5. The client core
(crates/client) and the browser terminal layer (web/) were moved from Kelpmux
at commit 7179aa3. The extracted and moved code remains the work of Joan
Fabregat and the Kelpmux contributors, under the same Apache-2.0 license.

KelpServer uses Alacritty's terminal engine and other Rust dependencies,
copyright their respective authors. Exact versions and license expressions
are recorded in Cargo.lock and the dependency metadata. KelpCore's
Apache-2.0 license does not replace those dependencies' licenses.

The browser layer is distributed as source; it bundles no third-party code.
Its file editor depends on CodeMirror 6 and Lezer (MIT, Marijn Haverbeke
and others), declared in package.json and installed by the consuming
application, which must ship their license texts with its build.
At runtime it loads assets the consuming application supplies: Chromium
libapps WASSH/WASI bindings (BSD) and the upstream OpenSSH WASM client, which
incorporates OpenSSL, zlib and ldns. Those assets and their license texts are
not part of this repository.

Native status-bar metrics incorporate code adapted from Vitals
(https://github.com/joanfabregat/vitals), Copyright (c) 2026 Joan Fabrégat,
licensed under MIT. The complete license is in assets/licenses/vitals-MIT.txt.

The file operations (crates/server/src/native/files.rs) adapt the design and
parts of the code of KelpHub's workspace file browser
(server/src/management/files.rs at commit ed69304), Copyright 2026 Joan
Fabregat, moved into KelpCore under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with
the copyright holder's approval.

The file browser and editor UI (web/src/files/: the request client, path
and document models, language detection, the CodeMirror editor and its
theme) is derived from KelpHub (web/src/files/ at commit 7057705),
Copyright 2026 Joan Fabregat, moved with the copyright holder's approval
into KelpCore under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
